      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-213245",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following relation defined on the set $A=\\{1,3,5,7\\}.$ \n\n$$\nR=\\{(1,3),(1,5),(3,5),(5,7)\\}\n$$\n\nSelect the options that make the following reasoning correct:\n\nWe have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(1,1){{field-1}}R,\\,(3,3){{field-2}}R,\\,(5,5){{field-3}}R,\\,(7,7){{field-4}}R\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since \n{{field-5}}{{field-6}}, \n\nthe relation is \n{{field-7}}."
